{"name":"Fields of Provence","hex":"#a491a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fields","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of field"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of field"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fields"}],"entries":[{"title":"Provence","blocks":[{"text":"Provence is a geographical, cultural region and historical province of southeastern France, which stretches from the left bank of the lower Rhône to the west to the Italian border to the east; it is bordered by the Mediterranean Sea to the south. It largely corresponds with the modern administrative region of Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur and includes the departments of Var, Bouches-du-Rhône, Alpes-de-Haute-Provence, as well as parts of Alpes-Maritimes and Vaucluse. The largest city of the region and its modern-day capital is Marseille."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Lavender_field_and_Mont_Ventoux.jpg/330px-Lavender_field_and_Mont_Ventoux.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Provence","wikidata":"Q101081"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/500px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/1280px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png/500px-Provence_in_France_%281789_borders_over_modern_Provence%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont